@moduledoc """
Tells the organization's `/integrations` pages that a source or a record changed
(`:integrations_updated` on `<%= inspect(@integrations) %>.topic/1`), after the
transaction. The page throttles its reloads, so a large delivery is cheap.

Only for actions that run in their own transaction: inside someone else's, an
`after_transaction` hook runs before that transaction commits (and Ash warns).
`<%= inspect(@integrations) %>.ingest/2`, which creates records and touches the source in
one transaction, announces the change itself once it has committed.
"""

use Ash.Resource.Change

alias <%= inspect(@integrations) %>

@impl true
def change(changeset, _opts, _context) do
  Ash.Changeset.after_transaction(changeset, fn
    _changeset, {:ok, %{organization_id: organization_id}} = result ->
      Integrations.announce(organization_id)
      result

    changeset, :ok ->
      Integrations.announce(changeset.data.organization_id)
      :ok

    _changeset, result ->
      result
  end)
end
